"note": "@phine_lukas @phine_stefan \n\nBonus issue:\n\nWhen hacking a pre-compiled version of `bpftool` like I do on `openshift build`, I saw your 2nd problem:\n\n```\n./build_upf --clean --Verbose --build-type Release --jobs\n...\n[ 20%] Building C object upf_app/bpf/CMakeFiles/far_ebpf_xdp.dir/far_ebpf_xdp_prgrm_kernel.c.o\nIn file included from /home/ubuntu/oai-cn5g-upf/src/upf_app/bpf/far_ebpf_xdp_prgrm_kernel.c:2:\nIn file included from /home/ubuntu/oai-cn5g-upf/src/upf_app/include/types.h:4:\n/usr/include/linux/types.h:5:10: fatal error: 'asm/types.h' file not found\n#include <asm/types.h>\n         ^~~~~~~~~~~~~\n1 error generated.\nmake[3]: *** [upf_app/bpf/CMakeFiles/far_ebpf_xdp.dir/build.make:76: upf_app/bpf/CMakeFiles/far_ebpf_xdp.dir/far_ebpf_xdp_prgrm_kernel.c.o] Error 1\nmake[2]: *** [CMakeFiles/Makefile2:442: upf_app/bpf/CMakeFiles/far_ebpf_xdp.dir/all] Error 2\nmake[1]: *** [CMakeFiles/Makefile2:265: CMakeFiles/upf.dir/rule] Error 2\nmake: *** [Makefile:169: upf] Error 2\nupf compilation failed\n```\n\nI did this : `sudo apt-get install gcc-multilib` and it seems to be working\n\nSee `https://gitlab.eurecom.fr/oai/cn5g/oai-cn5g-upf/-/merge_requests/27/diffs?commit_id=d6ae5e7da7236fbdca081c6af320eedc5c971ea0`",
"note_html": "<p data-sourcepos=\"1:1-1:27\" dir=\"auto\"><a href=\"/phine_lukas\" data-reference-type=\"user\" data-user=\"11197\" data-container=\"body\" data-placement=\"top\" class=\"gfm gfm-project_member js-user-link\" title=\"Lukas Rotheneder\">@phine_lukas</a> <a href=\"/phine_stefan\" data-reference-type=\"user\" data-user=\"10799\" data-container=\"body\" data-placement=\"top\" class=\"gfm gfm-project_member js-user-link\" title=\"Stefan Spettel\">@phine_stefan</a></p>\n<p data-sourcepos=\"3:1-3:12\" dir=\"auto\">Bonus issue:</p>\n<p data-sourcepos=\"5:1-5:104\" dir=\"auto\">When hacking a pre-compiled version of <code data-sourcepos=\"5:41-5:47\">bpftool</code> like I do on <code data-sourcepos=\"5:64-5:78\">openshift build</code>, I saw your 2nd problem:</p>\n<div class=\"gl-relative markdown-code-block js-markdown-code\">\n<pre data-sourcepos=\"7:1-22:3\" class=\"code highlight js-syntax-highlight language-plaintext\" lang=\"plaintext\" v-pre=\"true\"><code><span id=\"LC1\" class=\"line\" lang=\"plaintext\">./build_upf --clean --Verbose --build-type Release --jobs</span>\n<span id=\"LC2\" class=\"line\" lang=\"plaintext\">...</span>\n<span id=\"LC3\" class=\"line\" lang=\"plaintext\">[ 20%] Building C object upf_app/bpf/CMakeFiles/far_ebpf_xdp.dir/far_ebpf_xdp_prgrm_kernel.c.o</span>\n<span id=\"LC4\" class=\"line\" lang=\"plaintext\">In file included from /home/ubuntu/oai-cn5g-upf/src/upf_app/bpf/far_ebpf_xdp_prgrm_kernel.c:2:</span>\n<span id=\"LC5\" class=\"line\" lang=\"plaintext\">In file included from /home/ubuntu/oai-cn5g-upf/src/upf_app/include/types.h:4:</span>\n<span id=\"LC6\" class=\"line\" lang=\"plaintext\">/usr/include/linux/types.h:5:10: fatal error: 'asm/types.h' file not found</span>\n<span id=\"LC7\" class=\"line\" lang=\"plaintext\">#include &lt;asm/types.h&gt;</span>\n<span id=\"LC8\" class=\"line\" lang=\"plaintext\">         ^~~~~~~~~~~~~</span>\n<span id=\"LC9\" class=\"line\" lang=\"plaintext\">1 error generated.</span>\n<span id=\"LC10\" class=\"line\" lang=\"plaintext\">make[3]: *** [upf_app/bpf/CMakeFiles/far_ebpf_xdp.dir/build.make:76: upf_app/bpf/CMakeFiles/far_ebpf_xdp.dir/far_ebpf_xdp_prgrm_kernel.c.o] Error 1</span>\n<span id=\"LC11\" class=\"line\" lang=\"plaintext\">make[2]: *** [CMakeFiles/Makefile2:442: upf_app/bpf/CMakeFiles/far_ebpf_xdp.dir/all] Error 2</span>\n<span id=\"LC12\" class=\"line\" lang=\"plaintext\">make[1]: *** [CMakeFiles/Makefile2:265: CMakeFiles/upf.dir/rule] Error 2</span>\n<span id=\"LC13\" class=\"line\" lang=\"plaintext\">make: *** [Makefile:169: upf] Error 2</span>\n<span id=\"LC14\" class=\"line\" lang=\"plaintext\">upf compilation failed</span></code></pre>\n<copy-code></copy-code>\n</div>\n<p data-sourcepos=\"24:1-24:75\" dir=\"auto\">I did this : <code data-sourcepos=\"24:15-24:47\">sudo apt-get install gcc-multilib</code> and it seems to be working</p>\n<p data-sourcepos=\"26:1-26:130\" dir=\"auto\">See <code data-sourcepos=\"26:6-26:129\">https://gitlab.eurecom.fr/oai/cn5g/oai-cn5g-upf/-/merge_requests/27/diffs?commit_id=d6ae5e7da7236fbdca081c6af320eedc5c971ea0</code></p>",
"body_first_line_html": "<p><a href=\"/phine_lukas\" data-reference-type=\"user\" data-user=\"11197\" class=\"gfm gfm-project_member js-user-link\" title=\"Lukas Rotheneder\">@phine_lukas</a> <a href=\"/phine_stefan\" data-reference-type=\"user\" data-user=\"10799\" class=\"gfm gfm-project_member js-user-link\" title=\"Stefan Spettel\">@phine_stefan</a>...</p>",
